# SVG only — no README rendering, so the full shape vocabulary is available.
#
# A ladder rather than a cycle, because `originalPathFor` strips EXACTLY ONE prefix: from the
# twice-evicted path it climbs to the once-evicted one, not to the live one. Drawing a single return
# edge to the live path would assert the opposite. Down is a git mv inside a commit; up is a pure
# function of the path, which is why the up edges are dashed.
#
# The example path is short because the site's 30em measure caps a figure at its own width, and the
# twice-evicted label is the widest thing in this drawing.
...@_register

direction: down

live: "notes/x.html" {class: record}
once: "archive/2026/notes/x.html" {class: record}
twice: "archive/2027/archive/2026/notes/x.html" {class: record}

live -> once: archivePathFor
once -> twice: archivePathFor
twice -> once: originalPathFor {class: derives}
once -> live: originalPathFor {class: derives}
